# Files the template-sync workflow must never overwrite in derived repos.
# Everything NOT listed here is treated as template-owned and kept in sync;
# conflicts with local edits surface in the sync PR for review. Files that
# exist only downstream (e.g. your src/ tree) are never touched by sync.
#
# Note: per actions-template-sync, this file itself is not synced — each
# derived repo owns its copy and may extend it with project-divergent paths.

# Replaced per project (seed lives in docs/README.template.md)
README.md

# Customized on day 0 with real owners
.github/CODEOWNERS

# Gains project-specific variables downstream
.env.example

# May be relicensed per project
LICENSE

# Project web app (Upskill example-page redesign) — owned downstream, never sync
site/
netlify.toml
docs/upskill/

# Workflow files are synced per file, not excluded wholesale.
#
# This directory used to be excluded entirely, on the premise that "the project
# intentionally stores no PAT secret" and so could never push .github/workflows/*.
# That premise is gone — TEMPLATE_SYNC_TOKEN is configured on this repo, and
# template-sync now pushes workflow changes like any other file.
#
# The exclusion outlived its reason and became the problem it was hiding: with
# every workflow excluded, template fixes never arrived here. This repo sat on
# codeql-action 4.37.3 while the rest of the fleet moved to 4.37.8, pages.yml
# drifted onto floating tags while every other repo SHA-pins, and the seven
# stale Dependabot PRs cleared in Aug 2026 were all hand-patching what sync
# should have delivered.
#
# What stays excluded below is only what genuinely differs downstream. Each entry
# names why, so the next person can tell a real divergence from stale drift.

# A different workflow that happens to share the template's filename. The
# template publishes docs/explainer/; this publishes the site/ web app, with
# `enablement: true` so first run turns Pages on. Not a drifted copy — do not sync.
.github/workflows/pages.yml

# Downstream-only: no counterpart in the template.
.github/workflows/web-ci.yml

# Deliberately stricter than the template. The template uses run_or_skip, so a
# freshly stamped repo with no hook scripts does not go red before it has written
# any CI. This repo HAS those scripts, so a missing one is a real failure and
# run_or_fail is correct here. Syncing would silently weaken the gate.
.github/workflows/ci.yml

# Carries downstream path filters the template lacks — the scan also triggers on
# .trivyignore and on the workflow itself. That is an improvement worth having
# upstream; until it is ported to the template, syncing would delete it.
# TODO: port the path filters to claude_template_repo, then drop this entry so
# the upload-sarif pin stops lagging behind the fleet.
.github/workflows/container-scan.yml
